[package-declaration] Define platform-free package declaration (planning)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; Cargo.toml; crates/**
Do: Specify package identity/version, assets, persistence/schema requirements, host-version compatibility, and render-vocabulary capability requirements without target declarations.
Accept: A package declares what it needs semantically; no package field names an OS, architecture, window system, GPU backend, or target triple; and the declaration can be consumed by nworlds test/run/package.
-> game-contract
---
[render-batch] Define minimal host-owned renderer-agnostic RenderBatch (planning)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/rendering-contract.md; crates/engine-presentation/**; crates/engine-api/**
Do: Specify the smallest host-owned draw vocabulary consumed by game render production from GameState + Tau. Define ownership, lifetime, Send/'static requirements where needed, fire-and-forget submission, and target RenderSink translation without importing wgpu or platform commands.
Accept: GameState + Tau is the only render-production input; RenderBatch is owned and disposable; no journal, worldline, Orchestrator, input, branch selector, device, or host-clock value can enter the batch; and a target sink can translate the batch to backend instructions.
-> game-contract
---
[composition] Define generated static target composition (planning)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/presentation-host.md; .github/**; crates/**
Do: Specify whether nworlds generates a small static composition crate or selects a generic host executable, while keeping generated target details outside the game package and avoiding a plugin ABI in the first contract.
Accept: One composition mechanism is selected; the game package has no target entrypoint; generated composition owns target adapters; and the mechanism supports nworlds run and nworlds package.
-> game-contract
-> package-declaration
-> render-batch
---
[resolution] Define profile and runtime resolution (planning)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/platform-support-matrix.md; support.vine
Do: Separate static TargetProfile recipes from actual RuntimeCapabilities and define TargetResolution as adapter selection or an explicit unsupported result.
Accept: Build-time selection, distribution-time artifact selection, and runtime capability detection are distinct; unsupported environments report required/available capabilities and remediation at the host boundary; and games do not branch on target identity.
-> composition
-> package-declaration
