[migration-gate] Classify and gate existing proof code (planning)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; host.vine; crates/caravan-demo/**; crates/nworlds-desktop/**
Do: Classify the existing Caravan desktop wgpu implementation as historical proof/client code and define the migration sequence after the contract tasks complete. Keep the target-local proof client outside the game package and target-factory contract; do not promote it into the factory before GamePackage, HostContract, RenderBatch, composition, and resolution decisions are settled.
Accept: No current proof detail is silently promoted to the target-factory contract; no game package contains target selection; the migration has one owner and acceptance path; and the target-local proof client remains independently buildable while the factory boundary is settled.
